ref='Accessible feedback communicates meaning and supports the next action through usable text, controls and programmatic relationships. Main room-form barrier is a red border with no error text or associated label. Added fictional input rule: one ASCII uppercase letter then one ASCII digit; A1 passes format, a1/A11 fail. Provide visible associated Room ID label, exact error/correction text, associated description/invalid state when needed and keyboard-operable recovery with visible focus. Format acceptance does not mean access, room existence or booking. Separate picture adds “More explanation needed”, a labelled focusable explanation link and exposed status; specify the missing reasoning when possible. Orange without text/labels remains colour-only. The supplied investigation designs/inspects a paper or approved local form with no live service. Record actual keyboard activation, focus, zoom/reflow and relevant assistive-technology checks only when performed; otherwise mark not run. A checker or one keyboard path is not a full accessibility or user evaluation. Preserve permitted non-sensitive inputs and minimized evidence, not secrets or private learner records.'
